# Dialog Components

## Modal Dialog Components

### Basic Dialog
```typescript
import {
  Dialog,
  DialogContent,
  DialogDescription,
  DialogHeader,
  DialogTitle,
  DialogTrigger,
} from "@/components/ui/dialog"

<Dialog>
  <DialogTrigger asChild>
    <Button variant="outline">Open Dialog</Button>
  </DialogTrigger>
  <DialogContent className="bg-surface-lighter">
    <DialogHeader>
      <DialogTitle className="text-xl font-semibold text-content-darker">
        Dialog Title
      </DialogTitle>
      <DialogDescription className="text-sm text-content-light">
        Dialog description here.
      </DialogDescription>
    </DialogHeader>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

### Usage Guidelines
1. Use for important user interactions and confirmations
2. Keep content focused and concise
3. Include clear call-to-action buttons
4. Provide escape mechanisms (close button, overlay click)
5. Show proper loading states during actions
6. Handle form submissions appropriately
7. Maintain consistent styling

### Accessibility Considerations
- Trap focus within dialog when open
- Support keyboard navigation (Escape to close)
- Provide proper ARIA roles and labels
- Ensure proper focus management
- Include screen reader announcements
- Support reduced motion preferences

### Dialog Variants

#### Confirmation Dialog
```typescript
<Dialog>
  <DialogContent>
    <DialogHeader>
      <DialogTitle>Confirm Action</DialogTitle>
      <DialogDescription>
        Are you sure you want to proceed? This action cannot be undone.
      </DialogDescription>
    </DialogHeader>
    <div className="flex justify-end gap-2 mt-4">
      <Button variant="outline" onClick={onCancel}>
        Cancel
      </Button>
      <Button variant="destructive" onClick={onConfirm}>
        Delete
      </Button>
    </div>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

#### Form Dialog
```typescript
<Dialog>
  <DialogContent className="sm:max-w-[425px]">
    <DialogHeader>
      <DialogTitle>Edit Profile</DialogTitle>
      <DialogDescription>
        Make changes to your profile here.
      </DialogDescription>
    </DialogHeader>
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
      <div className="space-y-4 py-4">
        <div className="space-y-2">
          <Label htmlFor="name">Name</Label>
          <Input id="name" />
        </div>
        <div className="space-y-2">
          <Label htmlFor="email">Email</Label>
          <Input id="email" type="email" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <DialogFooter>
        <Button type="submit">Save changes</Button>
      </DialogFooter>
    </form>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

### Best Practices
1. Use appropriate dialog size for content
2. Implement proper error handling
3. Show validation feedback immediately
4. Include loading states for actions
5. Handle long content gracefully
6. Consider mobile viewports
7. Maintain consistent button placement

### Styling Guidelines
1. Use consistent padding and spacing
2. Apply proper typography hierarchy
3. Implement clear visual hierarchy
4. Use appropriate animations
5. Style form elements consistently
6. Handle focus states properly
7. Maintain proper z-index stacking# Dialog Components

